  "live_records": {
    "q-142541": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142541",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{19},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.9.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $19$ | $1.328$ | $1.729$ | $2.093$ | $2.539$ | $2.861$ |\n| $20$ | $1.325$ | $1.725$ | $2.086$ | $2.528$ | $2.845$ |\n| $21$ | $1.323$ | $1.721$ | $2.080$ | $2.518$ | $2.831$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X\\ge x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.9 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{19},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=19.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $19$ | $1.328$ | $1.729$ | $2.093$ | $2.539$ | $2.861$ |\n| $20$ | $1.325$ | $1.725$ | $2.086$ | $2.528$ | $2.845$ |\n| $21$ | $1.323$ | $1.721$ | $2.080$ | $2.518$ | $2.831$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 1.328)=0.100.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.328.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
