    "q-142580": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142580",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{25},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.995.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X\\ge x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.995 \\\\  & =0.005\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{25},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=25.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.787)=0.005.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.787.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
