    "q-142729": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142729",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{25},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.01.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198128/assets/635de7075b0d106ffc2a0f15e65ca7a3406a49945591aa5eae59090c74df1398.png)\n\nDue to the symmetry of the student's $t$-distribution, we have that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.01$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2P(X\\ge x)=0.01\\,⟹\\,P(X\\ge x)=0.005.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{25},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=25.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.787)=0.005.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.787.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
